# Kor, Cause of Vengeance: the sacrifice is optional (CR 608.2d), and the draw and the pump are the "if you do" and the
# "then" that follow it (CR 608.2c), so declining sacrifices nothing, draws nothing and pumps nobody - Kor is still 4/4.
# The last part checks the pump is "until end of turn" (CR 611.2a): on Bot2's next turn Kor is back to 4/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Kor, Cause of Vengeance
Burnout Bashtronaut
Black Lotus x4
Black Lotus x30

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Cast(Spend: B, B, R, W)
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Burnout Bashtronaut.Cast(Spend: R)
Bot1.Attack(Kor, Cause of Vengeance > Bot2; Burnout Bashtronaut > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
# Declining: the Burnout Bashtronaut is there and could be sacrificed ("another creature"), and Bot1 does not.
Bot1.Choose
? Bot1.Battlefield.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Power = 4
? Bot1.Battlefield.Burnout Bashtronaut.Power = 1

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Kor, Cause of Vengeance.Toughness = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Burnout Bashtronaut.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Burnout Bashtronaut.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
